; selftest-throwcharge.eval - handed to the runner by `Eval.ps1 -SelfTest`; must
; PASS, and the self-test reads its two `torch` readouts.
;
; A THROWN TORCH KEEPS ITS CHARGE (code-review C447). The console's `throw`
; dropped the held item's charge, so a part-burnt torch landed with its whole
; burn_time back. Crypt1's wall torch at 4,3 (north) is the way onto the cursor:
; Brand's bare hand takes the bracket's own torch, a torch with 30 s left goes
; into the bare bracket, and with both his hands full the second take lands on
; the cursor. Thrown at the wall it came off, it comes down in the party's own
; square and must lie there with no more than the 30 s it went up with - a fresh
; one reads close to torch_lit's 900.
logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
goto crypt1
freeze on
tp 4 3
face n
torch take
torch mount torch_lit 30
torch take
torch
throw
step 2
torch floor
state
